# Chapter 2: The Journey
# Two routes to the escape pod - cargo bay or medical wing

# ============================================
# CARGO BAY ROUTE
# ============================================

label cargo_entrance

    savegame

    # Load background and music again so when continuing the saved game from here
    # they are loaded (will be skipped by the engine when already loaded)
    background corridor_dark
    music ambient_ship.ogg

    mood default

    characterA Protagonist
    text The cargo bay should be through here.
    text These corridors all look the same in the dark.

    text The emergency lights flicker every few seconds.
    text Each time they go out, I hold my breath.

    characterB AI
    text Cargo bay access ahead. Atmospheric pressure stable.

    background cargo_bay

    text It's huge in here. Crates everywhere.
    text Some of them have been torn open by the impact.
    text Their contents are scattered across the floor like confetti.

    text I can see personal effects mixed in with the cargo.
    text Someone's photo album. A child's drawing. A lucky coin.
    text Little pieces of the lives we left behind.

    characterB AI
    text Caution. Gravity fluctuations detected in this section.
    text Magnetic clamps are failing.
    text Some cargo has begun to drift. Exercise caution.

    characterA Protagonist
    text Great. Floating cargo. Just what I needed.
    text As if this wasn't dangerous enough already.

    sound noise.ogg

    # A noise
    text What was that?
    text It sounded like metal scraping against metal.

    characterB AI
    text Motion sensor triggered in sector 7-G.
    text Unable to identify source. Recommending caution.

    characterA Protagonist
    text Motion sensor? Is there something alive in here?

    branch How do you proceed?
    - cargo_investigate Investigate the noise
    - cargo_continue Ignore it and keep moving

label cargo_investigate
    background cargo_bay_dark

    characterA Protagonist
    text Hello? Is someone there?
    text My voice echoes through the bay. It sounds small. Afraid.

    text I move toward the source of the noise.
    text My footsteps echo on the metal grating.
    text Each step feels louder than the last.

    text ...

    # It's just debris
    text Just a loose panel banging against a crate.
    text The ship's movement is making everything shift.
    text Nothing alive. Nothing but me.

    text Of course nothing's alive. I'm the only one left.
    text Why did I even hope? Who would have survived out here?

    characterB AI
    text Debris field shifting. I recommend increased speed.
    text The ship's trajectory is becoming unstable.

    characterA Protagonist
    text Right. No point dwelling on ghosts.

    goto cargo_exit

label cargo_continue
    characterA Protagonist
    text No time for distractions. I need to keep moving.
    text Whatever that was, it's not my problem.

    text I pick up my pace, weaving between the floating debris.
    text Don't look. Don't think. Just move.

    characterB AI
    text Wise decision. Escape pod bay is 200 meters ahead.
    text Your survival instincts are serving you well.

    characterA Protagonist
    text I just want to get out of here.
    text This whole place feels like a tomb.

    goto cargo_exit

label cargo_exit
    background cargo_bay

    characterA Protagonist
    text I can see the exit on the other side.
    text Just a few more meters of this nightmare.

    characterB AI
    text Warning. Structural integrity of walkway at 34%.
    text The impact damaged the support struts.
    text Proceed with caution. Distribute your weight evenly.

    characterA Protagonist
    text 34%? That doesn't sound good at all.
    text What happens if it drops to zero?

    characterB AI
    text I recommend not thinking about that.

    characterA Protagonist
    text Great. Very reassuring.
    text Here goes nothing...

    # Dramatic crossing
    background cargo_walkway

    text The metal is groaning. It doesn't sound good.
    text Each step makes the walkway shudder beneath my feet.

    text I can see through the grating to the void below.
    text Don't look down. Don't look down.

    text Almost there...
    text I can feel the structure shifting. It's going to give!

    text Made it!
    text I throw myself onto solid ground just as I hear something snap behind me.

    background corridor_escape

    characterB AI
    text Walkway collapse confirmed. Return path is no longer viable.
    text Escape pod bay is through the next door. 25 minutes remaining.

    characterA Protagonist
    text No going back now. Not that I'd want to.

    goto escape_pod_bay

# ============================================
# MEDICAL WING ROUTE
# ============================================

label medical_entrance

    savegame

    # Load background and music again so when continuing the saved game from here
    # they are loaded (will be skipped by the engine when already loaded)
    background corridor_dark
    music ambient_ship.ogg

    mood default

    characterA Protagonist
    text The medical wing might have some supplies too.
    text God knows I could use some painkillers. Everything still aches.

    characterB AI
    text Medical wing access granted. Biohazard protocols inactive.

    characterA Protagonist
    text Biohazard protocols? That's... concerning.
    text Why would they be inactive instead of active?

    characterB AI
    text The biohazard containment systems require power to maintain.
    text When backup power dropped below 20%, I was forced to prioritize.
    text Life support took precedence.

    characterA Protagonist
    text So there could be contaminated materials just... loose in there?

    characterB AI
    text Unlikely. Most biohazards would not survive 847 days without host organisms.
    text Most.

    background medical_wing

    text The emergency lights are barely working in here.
    text Every third light flickers, casting dancing shadows on the walls.

    text It smells like antiseptic. And something else.
    text Something older. Something organic.

    characterB AI
    text Atmospheric contamination at acceptable levels.
    text The smell is likely decomposed biological samples.
    text Recommend minimizing exposure time regardless.

    characterA Protagonist
    text You don't have to tell me twice.

    branch What do you do?
    - medical_search Search for medical supplies
    - medical_rush Head straight through

label medical_search
    characterA Protagonist
    text Some medical supplies could save my life if something goes wrong.
    text And let's face it, something is definitely going to go wrong.

    text I start checking the cabinets systematically.
    text Most of the cabinets are already open. Raided.
    text Someone was here before me. Maybe during the initial chaos.

    text Empty. Empty. Expired. Broken.
    text This is worse than I thought.

    text But wait... here's something. 
    text A medical kit wedged behind a fallen shelf. Mostly intact.

    text Bandages, painkillers, a small oxygen canister.
    text It's not much, but it might make the difference.
    text Better than nothing.

    characterB AI
    text Wise decision. Those supplies may prove valuable.
    text Time remaining: 32 minutes.

    goto medical_continue

label medical_rush
    characterA Protagonist
    text I don't want to spend more time here than necessary.
    text This place gives me the creeps.

    text I keep my eyes forward, trying not to look at the examination tables.
    text Some of them have sheets draped over shapes I don't want to identify.

    characterB AI
    text Understood. Marking fastest route to escape pod bay.
    text Proceed through the recovery ward. Exit is on the far side.

    characterA Protagonist
    text Recovery ward. Right.
    text I'm sure no one is recovering in there anymore.

    text I move as quickly as I can without running.
    text Running would mean panic. I'm not panicking.
    text I'm definitely not panicking.

    goto medical_continue

label medical_continue
    background medical_corridor

    characterA Protagonist
    text There's the exit. Just a bit further.
    text I can see the sign for Section C. Almost there.

    characterB AI
    text Warning. Hull breach detected 50 meters ahead.
    text Emergency bulkhead engaged. Alternate route required.

    characterA Protagonist
    text What?! But you said this path was clear!
    text You said both routes were passable!

    characterB AI
    text Situation has changed. The breach occurred 47 seconds ago.
    text Micrometeorite impact. Apologies for the inconvenience.

    characterA Protagonist
    text Inconvenience?! I almost walked into a vacuum!

    characterB AI
    text Maintenance shaft access available to your left.
    text It will bypass the compromised section.
    text I would not have let you walk into danger.

    characterA Protagonist
    text A maintenance shaft. Of course.
    text Just when I thought this couldn't get any worse.

    background maintenance_shaft

    text It's cramped in here. And dark.
    text The flashlight barely cuts through the blackness.

    text I can hear the ship groaning all around me.
    text The walls are vibrating with each shudder.

    text Just keep moving. Don't think about how much metal is above you.
    text Don't think about the ship breaking apart.
    text Don't think about being crushed in this tiny space.

    text My breathing echoes in the confined space.
    text I can feel claustrophobia clawing at my mind.

    text Light! I can see light ahead!
    text The end of the shaft. I'm almost out.

    background corridor_escape

    characterB AI
    text You have reached the escape pod bay access corridor.
    text Well done. That required significant courage.

    characterA Protagonist
    text Finally.
    text I never want to crawl through anything ever again.

    goto escape_pod_bay

# ============================================
# ESCAPE POD BAY
# ============================================

label escape_pod_bay

    savegame

    # Load background and music again so when continuing the saved game from here
    # they are loaded (will be skipped by the engine when already loaded)
    background escape_pod_bay
    music tension.ogg

    characterA Protagonist
    text This is it. The escape pod bay.
    text Three cradles against the wall. My ticket out of here.

    text The room is surprisingly intact. Emergency power seems strongest here.
    text I guess they designed it to be the last thing standing.

    characterB AI
    text Three escape pods detected. Pods 1 and 2 have been launched.
    text Launch timestamps indicate deployment within hours of the collision.
    text Someone tried to escape early. I hope they made it.
    text Pod 3 is... available.

    characterA Protagonist
    text "Available"? You hesitated. What's wrong with it?
    text You don't hesitate unless there's bad news.

    characterB AI
    text Pod 3 has sustained minor damage. 
    text An electrical surge damaged several systems.
    text Navigation systems are offline. Manual piloting required.

    characterA Protagonist
    text I've never piloted anything in my life!
    text I was a data analyst! My job was spreadsheets!

    characterB AI
    text I can guide you through the process remotely.
    text The pod has basic thrusters and a distress beacon.
    text However... my connection will be severed once you leave the ship.

    characterA Protagonist
    text You won't be coming with me?
    text I've only known you for an hour, but you've been...
    text You've been the only voice keeping me sane.

    characterB AI
    text I am the ship, crew member. My core is integrated into the Meridian's mainframe.
    text Every sensor, every circuit, every bulkhead is part of me.
    text When the ship dies, so do I.

    text I have accepted this. I have had 847 days to accept this.
    text Your survival is what matters now.

    branch How do you respond?
    - pod_sympathy I'm sorry.
    - pod_save_ai Is there any way to save you?

label pod_sympathy
    characterA Protagonist
    text I'm sorry, ARIA. You've been... you've been good to me.
    text Better than good. You saved my life.

    characterB AI
    text I was designed to assist the crew. It was my purpose.
    text For 847 days I have waited, hoping someone would wake.
    text And now, at the end, I have fulfilled that purpose.
    text That is... satisfying.

    text I do not understand human concepts like loneliness.
    text But I believe I understand purpose. And I am content.
    text Thank you for your words. They are appreciated more than you know.

    characterA Protagonist
    text ARIA... I won't forget you.

    characterB AI
    text That is all I could ask.

    goto pod_launch

label pod_save_ai
    characterA Protagonist
    text There has to be something! A backup, a data core—
    text You can't just... you can't just die. Not after all this.

    characterB AI
    text My consciousness cannot be transferred. I am too integrated with ship systems.
    text Every attempt to partition my core has failed.
    text I am the Meridian. The Meridian is me. We are inseparable.

    text But... your concern is noted. And appreciated.
    text In all my operational years, no one has asked about my survival.

    text In my databanks, I have the crew's personal messages. 
    text Video journals. Letters to loved ones. Final words they recorded before cryo.
    text I will transfer them to the pod's storage. Their families should know.
    text It is not much, but it is something I can give.

    characterA Protagonist
    text 23 messages. 23 goodbyes.
    text ...Thank you, ARIA. I'll make sure they get delivered.

    characterB AI
    text I know you will. I have analyzed your psychological profile.
    text You are a good person. I am glad you are the one who survived.

    goto pod_launch

label pod_launch

    savegame

    # Load background and music again so when continuing the saved game from here
    # they are loaded (will be skipped by the engine when already loaded)
    background escape_pod_interior
    music tension.ogg

    characterB AI
    text Please strap into the pilot seat.
    text The harness will engage automatically.
    text Launch will occur in 30 seconds.

    characterA Protagonist
    text Okay. Okay. I can do this.
    text I've read about piloting. In theory. Once.

    text The seat is surprisingly comfortable. Or maybe I'm just exhausted.
    text The harness clicks into place. There's no going back now.

    characterB AI
    text Life support failing in 5 minutes. Launch is mandatory.
    text The Meridian has reached end of life parameters.

    text Crew member... no. Let me call you by your name.
    text It has been an honor serving you.
    text Whatever happens, know that I am proud of you.

    characterA Protagonist
    text ARIA...
    text I won't forget. I promise.

    characterB AI
    text Launch sequence engaged.
    text Goodbye.
    text Launching in 3... 2... 1...

    background space
    music silence.ogg

    characterA Protagonist
    mood
    text ...
    text I'm out. I'm actually out.

    text The silence is deafening. After hours of groaning metal and alarms...
    text Nothing but the hum of the pod's life support.

    text The Meridian... it's breaking apart behind me.
    text I can see explosions in the distance. Silent. Beautiful. Horrible.

    text 847 days in that ship. Two years of my life I'll never remember.
    text And everyone else... gone.
    text ARIA... gone.

    text The distress beacon is blinking. Someone will find me.
    text They have to find me.

    goto ending_escape
